-- 08 | easy | Diameter of Binary Tree
SELECT pg_temp.seed_coding($q$Trees$q$, 'easy', $q$Diameter of Binary Tree$q$, $q$The diameter is the number of EDGES on the longest path between any two nodes (the path need not pass through the root). Print it. The tree is given in level order, with 'null' marking a missing child (the same format LeetCode uses); your function receives the root node.

