-- 21 | hard | Binary Tree Maximum Path Sum
SELECT pg_temp.seed_coding($q$Trees$q$, 'hard', $q$Binary Tree Maximum Path Sum$q$, $q$A path is any sequence of nodes where each adjacent pair is connected by an edge; it may start and end anywhere and must contain at least one node. Print the largest possible sum of node values along a path. The tree is given in level order, with 'null' marking a missing child (the same format LeetCode uses); your function receives the root node.

Input Format:
- root: an integer n, then n space-separated tokens: the binary tree in level order, 'null' marks a missing child

