SELECT pg_temp.seed_coding($q$Trees$q$, 'hard', $q$Vertical Order Traversal$q$, $q$Give the root coordinate (row 0, column 0); a left child is at (row + 1, column - 1) and a right child at (row + 1, column + 1). Print the node values column by column from the leftmost column to the rightmost, one column per line. Inside a column, order nodes by row, and break ties on the same row by smaller value first. The tree is given in level order, with 'null' marking a missing child (the same format LeetCode uses); your function receives the root node.

